From: geoca <272055834+geocausa@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: wsa884x: avoid full cache dirty on runtime clock-stop

SP11 keeps the WSA884x supplies enabled and reset deasserted across runtime
PM, and the SoundWire slave advertises simple clock-stop support.  Marking
the entire regcache dirty at runtime suspend therefore treats an ordinary
clock-stop as hardware context loss.

This is especially costly on SP11: function tracing measures each full
WSA884x regcache replay at roughly 4.3-4.6 seconds, and one cold playback
currently performs one replay from runtime_resume plus another from the
SoundWire reattach path for each of two amplifiers.

Leave the map cache-only while suspended, but do not force every register
dirty.  Regmap already tracks writes made while the map is cache-only.
Real suspended-time control changes are therefore still
synchronized on resume.  Keep the existing UNATTACHED/ATTACHED full-restore
path unchanged as the conservative context-loss fallback.

This is an isolated candidate only; it is not deployed.

Signed-off-by: geoca <272055834+geocausa@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c
@@ -2604,8 +2604,17 @@
 {
 	struct regmap *regmap = dev_get_regmap(dev, NULL);
 
+	/*
+	 * Runtime PM only clock-stops the internal SoundWire link on SP11; the
+	 * WSA supplies and reset remain asserted and the codec advertises simple
+	 * clock-stop capability.  Do not mark the entire 390-entry cache dirty as
+	 * though hardware context had been lost.  Regmap already marks the cache
+	 * dirty for writes made while cache-only, so runtime_resume's sync still
+	 * flushes genuine suspended-time changes.  The SoundWire UNATTACHED ->
+	 * ATTACHED recovery path intentionally retains its full dirty-cache restore
+	 * as a conservative context-loss fallback.
+	 */
 	regcache_cache_only(regmap, true);
-	regcache_mark_dirty(regmap);
 
 	return 0;
 }
